WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.357
The solution groups the data by student and creates one aggregate expression for each course.

00:00:06.357 --> 00:00:14.387
The maximum function works here because the exercise assumes at most one grade per student and course combination.

00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:16.457
That assumption matters.

00:00:16.457 --> 00:00:23.977
If several grades existed for the same student and course, maximum would choose one value and hide the others.

00:00:23.977 --> 00:00:28.891
So always connect the aggregate choice to the expected grain of the source.
